# The combined form written without `gh pr edit`

Round 1 of #1905 (NEW-5). The first version of that check required the literal
`gh pr edit`, and both pr-reviewer wrappers write the flags with no command in
front of them — so the guard's own primary target was outside its reach, and
restoring the combined form in either wrapper passed.

What separates safe from dangerous is whether the two flags share one command.
That question does not need the command's name, so the guard must not ask for
it.
